in flask adding html code at each page is called as adding templates 

to add templates in flask we require the render_templates dependency

>>> @app.route("/")
>>>def home():
>>>  return render_templates("index.html")

this is how we can add html code to our webpage/function 

  conditions:
1.the html file is under templates folder 
2. the templates folder is under the same folder that of flasks code/ pytons code

we can also we the concept of dynamic programming under the section of the rendering_templates


code example :::

from flask import Flask , redirect,render_template,url_for
app=Flask(__name__)


@app.route("/")
def home():
    return render_template("index.html")

if __name__=="__main__":
    app.run()
